      "side": 1,
      "message": "I feel like bringing compileDex to the top doesn\u0027t solve the double nesting of ifs, right now we have\n```\nif kotlin {\n  if compileDex {\n    # fail\n  }\n  # handle kotlin\n} else if compileDex {\n  # handle compile dex\n} else ...\n```\n\nif I bring compileDex to the top it would be instead\n```\nif compileDex {\n  if kotlin {\n    # fail\n  } else {\n    # handle compile dex\n  }\n} else if kotlin {\n  # handle kotlin\n} else { ...\n```\nI don\u0027t know if it\u0027s any better... I went with the following, let me know what you think: \n```\nif kotlin \u0026\u0026 !compileDex {\n  # handle kotlin\n} else if kotlin \u0026\u0026 compileDex {\n  # fail\n} else if compileDex { // guaranteed that !kotlin\n  # handle compile dex\n} else {\n```",
